; claude: the base of the from-scratch graphics libraries of graphics/:
; the framebuffer (a grid of pixels in memory), drawing images onto it
; (Blit), and the switch between optimized and simple code (Opti). See
; docs/claude_notes/notes_2d.md.
;
; In the package tiny_libs (libs/README.md), as tiny_libs.graphics_core,
; like every graphics/ library: public, so that a program outside this
; repository can use it; here, the software backends' and the SVG
; pictures' (graphics/images/svg, which the browsers of appkit_browser
; read, in a browser too), pure OCaml. Like the other graphics/
; libraries, it depends on nothing of the Playground, only on plain
; numbers: points, colors, pixels.
(library
 (name graphics_core)
 (public_name tiny_libs.graphics_core)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries graphics_2d_geometry) ; Affine, for Blit
)
